{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey","id":1467163,"title":"Making Possessed and Claimed the most dangerous prey","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-08T07:53:56-08:00","id":1467163,"title":"Making Possessed and Claimed the most dangerous prey","content":"Regarding the claim that Storm Lords make that Claimed and Possessed are the most dangerous prey. What are some tricks that they can do that will indeed back up the claim (no pun intended) that Storm Lords make.<br /> <br /> During a battle, what would stop a spirit from possessing a body, and then re-animating the corpse of that same body (or another), once that body has been mauled by Uratha. Would this be a valid reason that the spirit would purposely want to push the Uratha into Kuruth (the spirit fights the pack, triggers Kuruth, gets mauled, then re-animates a corpse to finish off the pack once the rampage is done). Would the Storm Lords be extra vigilant to maintain their self control because of this?<br /> <br /> In addition, what stops a Spirit from possessing a Uratha directly? I am sure that Rage spirits would find it pretty easy to find Uratha to work their influence on and then start the process of claiming and possession.<br /> <br /> With regards to Claimed, what happens to the spirit when the host is destroyed? Does the Spirit &quot;die&quot;, or does it just get ejected to twilight, able to continue on it's merry way?<br /> <br /> Finally. I assume that a Claimed Host can use the Influences of the Spirit. Does this allow a spirit to creatively use this to form a cult of humans around it which can be then used as cannon fodder or lackies?<br /> <br /> What other tricks can be used by Claiming Spirits and Possessing spirits which are a creative use of their powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T09:25:52-08:00","id":1467171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the claim that Storm Lords make that Claimed and Possessed are the most dangerous prey. What are some tricks that they can do that will indeed back up the claim (no pun intended) that Storm Lords make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes every Uratha Tribe certainly likes to boast about their prey being the most dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During a battle, what would stop a spirit from possessing a body, and then re-animating the corpse of that same body (or another), once that body has been mauled by Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the biggest hamper would be the corpse requiring the open condition. A flame spirit that was claiming an arsonist will likely be unable to possess any random corpse. Additionally any corpse that has been mauled enough to eject a spirit is not going to be a valid target for possession again. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would this be a valid reason that the spirit would purposely want to push the Uratha into Kuruth (the spirit fights the pack, triggers Kuruth, gets mauled, then re-animates a corpse to finish off the pack once the rampage is done). Would the Storm Lords be extra vigilant to maintain their self control because of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly a interesting tactic if the spirit has the means to push the Uratha into Death Rage. The only downside would be the spirit is also a valid target during the death rage. Hell it might be the ONLY valid target if it foolishly pushes a packmate into Kuruth when only the Urathas packmates are present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, what stops a Spirit from possessing a Uratha directly? I am sure that Rage spirits would find it pretty easy to find Uratha to work their influence on and then start the process of claiming and possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. A spirit can possess or claim anything that has the right conditions. However it is extremely dangerous to attempt to claim a Forsaken werewolf that has a pack at their back. For one thing the Uratha can see spirits, even if they are attempting to be sneaky and staying on the other side of the gauntlet. For another Totems and Uratha, Storm Lords in particular, know the signs to look out for. So yes, spirits of Rage might attempt to do such a thing, but it is a risky endeavor to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Claimed, what happens to the spirit when the host is destroyed? Does the Spirit &quot;die&quot;, or does it just get ejected to twilight, able to continue on it's merry way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it is a traumatic thing being separated, but the Spirit survives and is ejected into twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally. I assume that a Claimed Host can use the Influences of the Spirit. Does this allow a spirit to creatively use this to form a cult of humans around it which can be then used as cannon fodder or lackies?</div> </div> </div> </div>While a claimed can indeed form cults and have access to the spirits Influences, they do lose access to manifestations and numina. They start to rely more on their dread powers as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other tricks can be used by Claiming Spirits and Possessing spirits which are a creative use of their powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessing friends, loved ones, etc. Storm Lords maintain a cold air because each is aware that some day they may have to put down a friend, family member, or lover all over some spirits spiteful vengeance. In addition, making your own dread powers for claimed is a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T09:40:13-08:00","id":1467172,"title":"","content":"Not quite what you are asking for, but <a href=\"https://enddaysengine.tumblr.com/post/638766158590394369/the-urged-chronicles-of-darkness\" target=\"_blank\">I wrote this bit on the Urged</a> a while back that may act as inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, what stops a Spirit from possessing a Uratha directly? I am sure that Rage spirits would find it pretty easy to find Uratha to work their influence on and then start the process of claiming and possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little to nothing other than time and werewolves being more away of spiritual influence than mortals. Note that there is a Helion-Claimed (Uriel) in Acro's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190874-the-twelve-days-of-wolfmas-compiled\">