"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">this in fact happens on screen at a point. The Pack even has quite a pleasant conversation with the spirits after they get punted back to Twilight. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally. I assume that a Claimed Host can use the Influences of the Spirit. Does this allow a spirit to creatively use this to form a cult of humans around it which can be then used as cannon fodder or lackies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:36:27-08:00","id":1467174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey?p=1467171#post1467171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Additionally any corpse that has been mauled enough to eject a spirit is not going to be a valid target for possession again.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a spirit can heal a corpse with essence. It would start at incapacitated and the spirit could bring it back to strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey?p=1467171#post1467171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only downside would be the spirit is also a valid target during the death rage. Hell it might be the ONLY valid target if it foolishly pushes a packmate into Kuruth when only the Urathas packmates are present.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if the spirit is ejected to twilight it could be safe. The only exception is that Bone Shadows have the power to strike spirits in twilight. If there is a scene of Kuruth however, the whole scene would be chaos. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:50:34-08:00","id":1467175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey#post1467163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the claim that Storm Lords make that Claimed and Possessed are the most dangerous prey. What are some tricks that they can do that will indeed back up the claim (no pun intended) that Storm Lords make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the same thing every other prey or antagonist does. A big improvement can be made just by playing them smart. That's really all it takes to upgrade Random Monster #2 to a named and dangerous character. A claimed hasn't lost all its knowledge of the spirit world and its dangers now that it has taken a physical form, and that act in itself can be a dangerous one, the mere creation of one potentially turning a loved one into an enemy more intelligent and socially adept than any mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> During a battle, what would stop a spirit from possessing a body, and then re-animating the corpse of that same body (or another), once that body has been mauled by Uratha. Would this be a valid reason that the spirit would purposely want to push the Uratha into Kuruth (the spirit fights the pack, triggers Kuruth, gets mauled, then re-animates a corpse to finish off the pack once the rampage is done). Would the Storm Lords be extra vigilant to maintain their self control because of this? </div> </div> </div>Nothing would stop it beyond their Essence pool and the added risk of potentially being killed because they stuck around. And sure, Storm Lords could be extra vigilant to avoid it, or to make sure that they drain a targets Essence reserves through the use of banes, or other attacks. Plus since it takes a while for all the Attributes to re-allocate you would be better off with a 'Animate Dead' Numina rather than repeatedly claiming corpses with 0 Social and Mental scores.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, what stops a Spirit from possessing a Uratha directly? I am sure that Rage spirits would find it pretty easy to find Uratha to work their influence on and then start the process of claiming and possession. </div> </div> </div>Nothing completely stops them, just about every supernatural can be claimed in second edition. But as noted above it can be difficult because werewolves can just see spirits in Twilight and from there can just work a binding or grab a bane and turn the tables easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With regards to Claimed, what happens to the spirit when the host is destroyed? Does the Spirit &quot;die&quot;, or does it just get ejected to twilight, able to continue on it's merry way? </div> </div> </div>It just gets ejected, yes, able to continue on its merry way, but if a sacred hunt has targeted it it's still hunted, and werewolves can just see spirits popping out in Twilight without needing to do anything special. From there you just need a whisper knife, or a bane (which is the same as it was for the claimed form).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally. I assume that a Claimed Host can use the Influences of the Spirit. Does this allow a spirit to creatively use this to form a cult of humans around it which can be then used as cannon fodder or lackies? </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's one of the ways they start cults. There's no reason it has to be limited to humans, either. They could have a pack of Ghost Wolves at their beck and call, or a coterie of vampires or cabal of mind-slaved mages. Claimed aren't forced to work alone, they can lure in weaker spirits and get them to claim things and gather a ton of claimed minions like the Devourer Hounds in the core. They don't even need to build something as unseemly as a cult, being capable of taking over more legitimate religious groups, companies or corporations, military units, law enforcement or criminal organizations, aspects of infrastructure from local waste management to national levels of governance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2021, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T14:14:54-08:00","id":1467723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1467163-making-possessed-and-claimed-the-most-dangerous-prey?p=1467174#post1467174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a spirit can heal a corpse with essence. It would start at incapacitated and the spirit could bring it back to strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it has enough essence to do so sure. But that requires it to have essence leftover after a fight with werewolves during it's possessed or claimed stage, as well as enough essence after to retry. Essence isn't infinite and it may be a far better option for it to use that essence in a bid to flee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}